# closure_borrows_unless_move - a closure written without `move` borrows each captured value that is not `Copy` (the variable stays usable and its own scope releases it once; each call reads it as it is then; the closure is `Copy`; held or temporary, the variable may be moved once the closure can no longer run), and a `move` closure owns what it captures and releases it once, where it is released or by the callee it is given to.
